WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
- Can we see another
car you have in there?

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.530
- This is my '55 Buick Roadmaster.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.713
When I came to Los Angeles,

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.610
I got off the plane at LAX,

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.827
I immediately went to the newsstand,

00:00:11.827 --> 00:00:13.710
and I bought a copy of The Penny Saver,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.150
that's like one of those
advertisement things,

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.730
you know, you buy things to sale.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.090
And I was looking for a car,

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.900
'cause in LA you need a car
before you need a place to live.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.690
'Cause you can't get a place
to live unless you get a car.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.690
So I saw this advertised for
350 bucks, and I bought it,

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.600
and I've had it since 1972.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.160
I met wife in this car,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.650
we dated in this car,

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:37.940
I got married in this car.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.720
I took this car to my first Tonight Show.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.493
I took it to my last Tonight Show.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.470
I'll tell you this story my wife hates,

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.260
my wife hates this story,

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.660
but it's kind of funny,

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.289
'cause we had our first
encounter in this car.

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:54.761
(laughs)

00:00:54.761 --> 00:00:55.974
- Encounter.

00:00:55.974 --> 00:00:56.807
(laughs)

00:00:56.807 --> 00:00:57.640
- Encounter.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.473
On our 25th wedding anniversary,

00:00:58.473 --> 00:01:00.710
I said "Let's try and recreate that."

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.010
So we both got in the car,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.230
and we drove to where
we had our encounter,

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.040
but now it's a housing development.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.300
So I'm like, "Okay, I think
it's right where that house is."

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.133
Okay.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.477
So we pull up the street, okay?

00:01:12.477 --> 00:01:15.160
And the house is like right there.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:19.943
So, you're not as agile
at 25 as you are at 50.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.285
(laughs)

00:01:23.285 --> 00:01:24.165
And then's it sound like,

00:01:24.165 --> 00:01:25.240
"Ow, my hair!",

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.310
and the horn's beeping,

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.317
it's like two o'clock in the morning,

00:01:28.317 --> 00:01:29.960
I see the porch light come on,

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.111
the guy comes running,
"What's going on out here?"

00:01:32.111 --> 00:01:33.960
Nothing, nothing, excuse me.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.220
And that then also, the second encounter

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.980
was not as successful
as the first encounter.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.730
But we had a lot of
laughs, it was pretty fun.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.750
- That's pretty much how
marriage goes though, right?

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.990
The second letter was different.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.130
(laughs)

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.250
Just kidding.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.210
- Exactly.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.070
- I'm just kidding.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.340
No that's awesome.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.790
I think you've found the love of your life

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:53.250
